  "term": "spaced practice",
  "definition": "Spaced practice is a way of organizing training so that practice sessions are distributed over time rather than grouped together in a massed format. In the source packet, it refers to one of two practice regimens used to compare whether spreading working memory updating training across time changed transfer effects.",
